     A*                                     D0611A - JUCLST4: order list
     A*                                     (JUCHUM), load-all
     A*                                     subfile with a row-selection option
     A*                                     (5 = call
     A*                                     F0604A, order inquiry - see
     A*                                     "DISCOVERED DEPENDENCY
     A*                                     MISMATCH" below: F0604A takes no
     A*                                     parameters, so no
     A*                                     customer code is actually passed).
     A*                                     Lesson 06-11.
     A*
     A*                                     CONFIRMED V1 (compile-check,
     A*                                     part06-screens-compile,
     A*                                     2026-09-26): CRTDSPF
     A*                                     Highest Severity 00.
     A*                                     Interactive subfile/EXFMT
     A*                                     execution (V3) is still
     A*                                     untested - SSH
     A*                                     non-interactive batches
     A*                                     cannot drive a real
     A*                                     5250 device (same
     A*                                     WORKSTN/EXFMT limitation
     A*                                     as 04-11 and
     A*                                     tk0100d.dspf; see
     A*                                     docs/probes.md).
     A*                                     Verify with a real 5250
     A*                                     session before relying
     A*                                     on this file's
     A*                                     interactive behavior.
     A*
     A*                                     COLUMN POSITIONS: base columns (6=A
     A*                                     literal,
     A*                                     17=name type, 19-28=name,
     A*                                     30-34=length, 35=type,
     A*                                     36-37=decimals, 38=usage, 39-41=row,
     A*                                     42-44=col,
     A*                                     45-=keyword) confirmed by CRTDSPF in
     A*                                     probe 04-11
     A*                                     (docs/probes.md).
     A*                                     SFL/SFLCTL/message-subfile
     A*                                     keyword usage below follows the
     A*                                     house pattern
     A*                                     already established in
     A*                                     src/legacy/qddssrc/tk0100d.dspf
     A*                                     (Part 5) and
     A*                                     tools/gen/dspf.mjs's SFL helper
     A*                                     functions - see
     A*                                     that file's own header for 4
     A*                                     documented gaps in
     A*                                     the original helper implementations
     A*                                     (sflRecordFormat
     A*                                     missing the mandatory record-level
     A*                                     SFL keyword,
     A*                                     sflPgmQ/errMsgId/sflRcdNbr wrong
     A*                                     argument shapes).
     A*                                     Worked around the same way
     A*                                     tk0100d.dspf works
     A*                                     around them: plain
     A*                                     recordFormat(name,'SFL') instead
     A*                                     of sflRecordFormat();
     A*                                     SFLPGMQ/SFLMSGKEY as bare
     A*                                     field-level keyword text via
     A*                                     field()'s kw param;
     A*                                     no ERRMSGID (not needed - see
     A*                                     message-subfile note
     A*                                     below). IMPORTANT: these
     A*                                     SFL-specific column
     A*                                     positions are THEMSELVES still
     A*                                     unverified on real
     A*                                     hardware -
     A*                                     verify/part05-gen-probe/src/t0sfl.ds
     A*                                     pf
     A*                                     (T0SFL) exercises them but has not
     A*                                     yet been run
     A*                                     per docs/probes.md. Verify with
     A*                                     CRTDSPF before
     A*                                     relying on this file, same as
     A*                                     tk0100d.dspf's own
     A*                                     header instructs.
     A*
     A*                                     NO DDS CONDITIONING INDICATORS (cols
     A*                                     7-16) are
     A*                                     used anywhere in this file, by the
     A*                                     same policy as
     A*                                     tk0100d.dspf: 04-11 tried
     A*                                     indicator-conditioned
     A*                                     output fields and failed to compile
     A*                                     (CPD7410/
     A*                                     CPD7606/CPD5238, docs/probes.md);
     A*                                     this file avoids
     A*                                     stacking that unresolved risk onto
     A*                                     the separately-
     A*                                     unverified SFL columns above.
     A*                                     SFLDSP/SFLDSPCTL on
     A*                                     SFL1CTL and MSGCTL below are
     A*                                     therefore always-on
     A*                                     (unconditioned), same tradeoff
     A*                                     tk0100d.dspf
     A*                                     documents: safe here because
     A*                                     f0611s.rpgle always
     A*                                     WRITEs at least one SFL1 record
     A*                                     before EXFMT (even
     A*                                     zero JUCHUM rows still goes through
     A*                                     a header-only
     A*                                     WRITE - see f0611s.rpgle's header
     A*                                     for how it avoids
     A*                                     the empty-subfile case IBM's SFLDSP
     A*                                     reference
     A*                                     warns about).
     A*
     A*                                     LOAD-ALL (this file's
     A*                                     primary/documented form, per
     A*                                     work/design/part06-design-v1.md's
     A*                                     B1-16
     A*                                     disposition: load-all is taught
     A*                                     first as the basic
     A*                                     form, page-at-a-time second as an
     A*                                     optimization).
     A*                                     SFLSIZ(9999) is a large fixed max so
     A*                                     f0611s.rpgle
     A*                                     can WRITE every JUCHUM row before
     A*                                     the first EXFMT
     A*                                     of SFL1CTL; SFLPAG(14) is only the
     A*                                     VISIBLE page
     A*                                     size (rows 5-18). Once all rows are
     A*                                     loaded,
     A*                                     ROLLUP(25)/ROLLDOWN(26) scrolling
     A*                                     within the
     A*                                     loaded subfile is handled entirely
     A*                                     by the system -
     A*                                     no RPG-side "more records" handling
     A*                                     is needed for
     A*                                     load-all (contrast with
     A*                                     page-at-a-time below).
     A*
     A*                                     PAGE-AT-A-TIME CONVERSION NOTE
     A*                                     (described here, not
     A*                                     implemented as a second file - see
     A*                                     task scoping):
     A*                                     (1) change SFLSIZ(9999) to
     A*                                     SFLSIZ(15) i.e.
     A*                                     SFLPAG+1 (the usual "one extra slot"
     A*                                     convention so
     A*                                     SFLEND's *MORE detection has a
     A*                                     record to test);
     A*                                     (2) f0611s.rpgle would WRITE only
     A*                                     the first
     A*                                     SFLPAG (14) JUCHUM rows before the
     A*                                     first EXFMT,
     A*                                     instead of every row; (3) after
     A*                                     EXFMT, on ROLLUP
     A*                                     (indicator 25/PAGEDOWN) with more
     A*                                     JUCHUM rows
     A*                                     still unread, the program would
     A*                                     WRITE one more
     A*                                     page's worth into the subfile
     A*                                     (continuing RRN)
     A*                                     before the next EXFMT, and stop
     A*                                     advancing once
     A*                                     READ on JUCHUM hits end-of-file; (4)
     A*                                     add SFLEND
     A*                                     (or SFLEND(*MORE)) to SFL1CTL,
     A*                                     conditioned so the
     A*                                     "+" more-records indicator only
     A*                                     shows while JUCHUM
     A*                                     is not yet exhausted. See
     A*                                     f0611s.rpgle's header
     A*                                     for the RPG-side half of this same
     A*                                     note.
     A*
     A*                                     MESSAGE SUBFILE (MSGSFL/MSGCTL
     A*                                     below): shows an
     A*                                     "invalid option" diagnostic when OPT
     A*                                     is neither
     A*                                     blank nor 5. Modeled on
     A*                                     tk0100d.dspf's MSGSFL/
     A*                                     MSGCTL pattern
     A*                                     (SFLMSGRCD/MSGKEY+SFLMSGKEY/PGMQ+
     A*                                     SFLPGMQ/SFLINZ/OVERLAY, no
     A*                                     SFLCLR/SFLEND - see
     A*                                     that file's header for the IBM
     A*                                     SFLINZ/SFLPGMQ
     A*                                     pairing requirement this reuses).
     A*                                     tk0100.rpg's own
     A*                                     header states it never actually
     A*                                     drives TK0100D's
     A*                                     SFL1/MSGSFL; f0611s.rpgle is this
     A*                                     repo's first RPG
     A*                                     program to actually drive a message
     A*                                     subfile, via
     A*                                     the free-form SND-MSG operation with
     A*                                     %TARGET(*SELF) (ilerpgref75.txt,
     A*                                     "SND-MSG (Send a
     A*                                     Message to the Joblog)") - see its
     A*                                     header for the
     A*                                     PGMQ='*' contract this DDS requires
     A*                                     of it.
     A*
     A*                                     CONTRACT with f0611s.rpgle: SFL1
     A*                                     fields (OPT/JUNO/
     A*                                     JUTOK/JUDATE/JUTAN) match JUCHUM's
     A*                                     own field names
     A*                                     (db/v1/juchum.pf) so WORKSTN/DB
     A*                                     field auto-match
     A*                                     fills JUNO/JUTOK/JUDATE/JUTAN
     A*                                     straight from a plain
     A*                                     assignment in the load loop; OPT is
     A*                                     this screen's
     A*                                     own selection field (usage B, not in
     A*                                     JUCHUM). RRN
     A*                                     for SFILE(SFL1:*) is an RPG-only
     A*                                     variable (no DDS
     A*                                     field needed - SFLRCDNBR is not used
     A*                                     here, same
     A*                                     "not in rpgConstructsUsed, omitted"
     A*                                     reasoning as
     A*                                     tk0100d.dspf). Option 5 -> CALL
     A*                                     F0604A.
     A*
     A*                                     DISCOVERED DEPENDENCY MISMATCH
     A*                                     (important - flagged
     A*                                     for the 06-04/06-11 lesson authors):
     A*                                     D0604A/F0604A
     A*                                     did NOT exist yet under src/qddssrc/
     A*                                     or
     A*                                     src/qrpglesrc/ when this file was
     A*                                     FIRST drafted;
     A*                                     they appeared mid-session (written
     A*                                     by a concurrent
     A*                                     sibling agent for lesson 06-04)
     A*                                     before this file was
     A*                                     committed, so f0611s.rpgle was
     A*                                     checked against the
     A*                                     REAL f0604s.rpgle instead of an
     A*                                     assumed interface.
     A*                                     That real program has NO *ENTRY
     A*                                     PLIST/dcl-pi at all
     A*                                     (dcl-f d0604a workstn; with no
     A*                                     parameters) - it is a
     A*                                     fully self-contained interactive
     A*                                     screen that prompts
     A*                                     for its OWN customer code via TOKCD
     A*                                     input on JUCFMT,
     A*                                     exactly like R0411A. It therefore
     A*                                     cannot actually
     A*                                     receive a passed customer code from
     A*                                     this list - the
     A*                                     original task brief's "call F0604A
     A*                                     passing that
     A*                                     row's customer code" is NOT
     A*                                     achievable against the
     A*                                     F0604A as actually written.
     A*                                     f0611s.rpgle calls it
     A*                                     with a zero-parameter dcl-pr
     A*                                     extpgm('F0604A')
     A*                                     prototype (same shape F0605A already
     A*                                     uses for
     A*                                     R0409A, which also has no *ENTRY
     A*                                     PLIST) and a plain
     A*                                     parameterless callp; the learner
     A*                                     will retype the
     A*                                     customer code on F0604A's own
     A*                                     screen. Giving F0604A
     A*                                     a real entry parameter would need a
     A*                                     dcl-pi *entry -
     A*                                     deliberately deferred to 06-12 by
     A*                                     this design's own
     A*                                     B1-16 disposition - so this is a
     A*                                     genuine, not just
     A*                                     cosmetic, cross-lesson design gap
     A*                                     for the syllabus
     A*                                     author to resolve (e.g. by rescoping
     A*                                     06-11's "passes
     A*                                     the customer code" claim, or by
     A*                                     revisiting 06-04's
     A*                                     dcl-pi timing).
     A*
     A*                                     NAMING NOTE: this repo's general S/A
     A*                                     object-suffix
     A*                                     convention (docs/style-guide.md,
     A*                                     "A-R = learner-
     A*                                     written, S-Z = distributed sample")
     A*                                     would suggest a
     A*                                     git file named d0611s.dspf compiles
     A*                                     to a sample
     A*                                     object ending in S (compare
     A*                                     c0511s.clp -> C0511S,
     A*                                     Part 5). However, the verify/
     A*                                     manifest format keeps
     A*                                     the git file name and the remote
     A*                                     member/object name
     A*                                     independent (each "file" step has
     A*                                     its own "member"
     A*                                     field, e.g.
     A*                                     verify/part05-legacy-probe/manifest.
     A*                                     json
     A*                                     compiles localPath tk0100d.dspf to
     A*                                     member TK0100D,
     A*                                     a different spelling) - and
     A*                                     f0604s.rpgle (the real,
     A*                                     already-written sibling file for
     A*                                     06-04) confirms the
     A*                                     object-name convention actually used
     A*                                     for Part 6's
     A*                                     WORKSTN files: its own "dcl-f d0604a
     A*                                     workstn;" line
     A*                                     names the file after the OBJECT
     A*                                     D0604A, not the git
     A*                                     filename d0604s.dspf. f0611s.rpgle
     A*                                     below follows the
     A*                                     same pattern ("dcl-f d0611a workstn
     A*                                     ...") - so this
     A*                                     repo's S/A-suffix rule already
     A*                                     applies exactly as
     A*                                     the task instructed (object
     A*                                     D0611A/F0611A), and no
     A*                                     naming conflict actually exists;
     A*                                     superseded by the
     A*                                     discovery above, kept here only as a
     A*                                     record of the
     A*                                     reasoning.
     A*
     A*                                     References checked this session:
     A*                                     ilerpgref75.txt -
     A*                                     SFILE(recformat:rrnfield) keyword
     A*                                     (~line 28400),
     A*                                     READC (~line 62000), CHAIN
     A*                                     search-argument forms
     A*                                     (~line 53190), SND-MSG (~line
     A*                                     64132); tools/gen/
     A*                                     dspf.mjs (SFL/SFLCTL helper
     A*                                     functions + header);
     A*                                     src/legacy/qddssrc/tk0100d.dspf
     A*                                     (house SFL/message-
     A*                                     subfile pattern); db/v1/juchum.pf
     A*                                     (field names/
     A*                                     lengths).
     A*
     A                                      DSPSIZ(24 80 *DS3)
     A          R SFL1                      SFL
     A            OPT            1A  B  4  2
     A            JUNO           6A  O  4  5
     A            JUTOK          6A  O  4 13
     A            JUDATE         8S 0O  4 21
     A            JUTAN          6A  O  4 31
     A          R SFL1CTL                   SFLCTL(SFL1)
     A                                      SFLSIZ(9999)
     A                                      SFLPAG(14)
     A                                      SFLDSP
     A                                      SFLDSPCTL
     A                                      ROLLUP(25)
     A                                      ROLLDOWN(26)
     A                                      CF03(03)
     A*                                     FIXED (part06-screens-compile
     A*                                     prep, 2026-09-26, based on the
     A*                                     confirmed real-hardware fix in
     A*                                     src/legacy/qddssrc/tk0100d.dspf
     A*                                     - docs/probes.md's part05-
     A*                                     legacy-probe section): a SFLCTL
     A*                                     record cannot carry positioned
     A*                                     output both above (title/column
     A*                                     headers) AND below (MORE/F3=
     A*                                     Exit) its own subfile - CPD7812
     A*                                     ("Subfile control record
     A*                                     overlaps subfile record"). Split
     A*                                     the footer into R SFL1FTR below;
     A*                                     added OVERLAY here so SFL1FTR's
     A*                                     own output survives once
     A*                                     SFL1CTL is (re)written on top of
     A*                                     it. f0611s.rpgle WRITEs SFL1FTR
     A*                                     immediately before each EXFMT
     A*                                     SFL1CTL.
     A                                      OVERLAY
     A                                  1  2'JUCLST4 - Order list (JUCHUM)'
     A                                  3  2'Op'
     A                                  3  5'Order#'
     A                                  3 13'Cust'
     A                                  3 21'Date'
     A                                  3 31'Rep'
     A*                                     SFL1FTR: split out of SFL1CTL
     A*                                     above (CPD7812 fix, see its
     A*                                     comment). MORE: F0611A MOVELs
     A*                                     'MORE...'/'BOTTOM' here,
     A*                                     same plain-output-field technique as
     A*                                     tk0100d.dspf
     A*                                     (stands in for SFLEND).
     A          R SFL1FTR
     A            MORE          10A  O 20  2
     A                                 23  2'F3=Exit  Roll=Page'
     A*                                     MSGSFL: message subfile detail line.
     A*                                     Same
     A*                                     recordFormat(name,'SFL') workaround
     A*                                     as SFL1 above
     A*                                     (dspf.mjs sflRecordFormat() gap).
     A          R MSGSFL                    SFL
     A*                                     SFLMSGRCD(24): messages grow upward
     A*                                     from line 24
     A*                                     (bottom of a 24-line screen), same
     A*                                     as tk0100d.dspf.
     A                                      SFLMSGRCD(24)
     A*                                     MSGKEY/PGMQ: field-level bare
     A*                                     keywords, not
     A*                                     sflPgmQ(name) - dspf.mjs gap #2,
     A*                                     same workaround
     A*                                     as tk0100d.dspf.
     A            MSGKEY                    SFLMSGKEY
     A            PGMQ                      SFLPGMQ
     A          R MSGCTL                    SFLCTL(MSGSFL)
     A                                      SFLSIZ(2)
     A                                      SFLPAG(1)
     A*                                     Unconditioned SFLDSP/SFLDSPCTL +
     A*                                     SFLINZ: same
     A*                                     MSGSFL-is-usually-empty reasoning as
     A*                                     tk0100d.dspf
     A*                                     (IBM SFLDSP reference: an output op
     A*                                     to an inactive
     A*                                     subfile errors; SFLINZ + field-level
     A*                                     SFLPGMQ below
     A*                                     keep MSGCTL active and rebuild
     A*                                     MSGSFL from PGMQ on
     A*                                     every write).
     A                                      SFLDSP
     A                                      SFLDSPCTL
     A                                      SFLINZ
     A*                                     OVERLAY: MSGCTL is written on top of
     A*                                     SFL1CTL without erasing it. FIXED
     A*                                     (part06-screens-compile prep,
     A*                                     2026-09-26): this keyword used to
     A*                                     sit after the PGMQ field line
     A*                                     below - CPD7486 ("Keyword
     A*                                     specified at incorrect level"),
     A*                                     same root cause and fix as
     A*                                     tk0100d.dspf's MSGCTL (see
     A*                                     docs/probes.md's part05-legacy-
     A*                                     probe section). Moved back above
     A*                                     PGMQ so it stays record-level.
     A                                      OVERLAY
     A            PGMQ                      SFLPGMQ
     A*                                     SFLCLR intentionally omitted:
     A*                                     f0611s.rpgle clears
     A*                                     old messages by not re-sending them,
     A*                                     not by
     A*                                     SFLCLR - same as tk0100d.dspf.
